"""Open-licensed substitute webfonts for the Serif design system, inlined.

Denim and Eliza are licensed commercial faces and must not be redistributed.
The Serif design system picks open stand-ins under the SIL Open Font License,
matched on set width, x-height, cap height and letter construction:

    Denim -> Figtree   at size-adjust 96%   (variable, covers 400 and 600)
    Eliza -> PT Serif  at size-adjust 104%

Source: design-system/fonts-open/ in the repo (fonts.css, OFL-*.txt).
License texts travel with the design system, not with this file.

serif_design.py imports FONT_CSS if this module is present and falls back to a
system stack if it is not, so the console still renders without it.
"""

FONT_CSS = """
@font-face{font-family:"Figtree";font-style:normal;font-weight:300 900;
  src:url(data:font/woff2;base64,) format("woff2");size-adjust:96%;font-display:swap}
@font-face{font-family:"PT Serif";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;
  src:url(data:font/woff2;base64,) format("woff2");size-adjust:104%;font-display:swap}
"""
